+# Rewards browser test build
+
+Isolated detached worktree based on a690322. Existing PR branches and their working trees are not modified. Diary's uncommitted work in another checkout is deliberately not incorporated.
+
+Scope: five-row dashboard; six-row category/ready browser with seven category shortcuts, group/filter/sort controls, 21 reward slots, conditional pagination, readable non-italic lore and time units, and one-click claims that retain the current view. No claim-all and no resource pack requirements.
+
+Constraints: reward IDs, criteria, action definitions, gold/IP policy, databases and the core claim path remain authoritative and unchanged. Unknown progress must not display as zero. Inventory buttons are resolved against a server-side holder; bottom-inventory items, dragging, hotbar swaps and rapid repeated clicks must not trigger claims. Reopening after an asynchronous completion is forbidden when the player has closed or changed menus.
+
+Verification: model, item renderer, and click/claim lifecycle regression tests; full clean Java 25 verification; isolated final-JAR SQLite read-only test. Live GUI appearance/behavior remains for user acceptance. No PRs, merges or server deployment.
+
+Completed local verification: 255 Java tests passed (including 22 GUI tests), zero failures/errors/skips; the final shaded JAR printed SHADED_SQLITE_READ_ONLY_OK. Test version 2.2.2-rewards-gui-test.1. The matching unchanged renderer is pilot.5. No live GUI/server acceptance is claimed.
